Done. `QUEUE_CAPACITY=unbounded` (any casing) now yields `Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY` via a new `capacityValue()` helper that leaves `positiveInt` untouched, and `createQueue` accepts Infinity as a valid capacity (`isFull` stays false, `enqueue` never throws `QueueFullError`). Added coverage for case-insensitive parsing, unchanged defaults/rejections, and unbounded size/enqueue/dequeue/drain/isFull behavior. All 33 tests pass with `node --test`; `src/app.js` and other files are untouched.
